{"parentUuid":"35cb1050-4fd7-46ee-b4bb-48fdd57aaf12","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a82031569a3b85bea","attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14832194 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"5ba7278d-2b12-4566-8f77-321c86155068","timestamp":"2026-09-29T16:26:27.045Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14832194 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1","slug":"warm-pondering-kernighan"}
{"parentUuid":"5ba7278d-2b12-4566-8f77-321c86155068","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a82031569a3b85bea","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfY3VEqTWyHp2RYGVWU3h","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"K-PROD review: 17 findings (1 blocker, 12 major, 4 minor). The most serious is that the milestone gate passes even though four of the six milestones cannot reach their own exit criteria. `check.py` is green (0 errors, 0 warnings), but it only checks that each skill's contract dependencies are available. It never checks a milestone against the configuration it names. Comparing the checker's own configuration membership with the skills available at each milestone, every milestone before M5 falls short:\n\n| Milestone | Promised exit | Skills missing by then |\n|---|---|---|\n| M1 | indie-2d game shippable | Console, mobile and web platform skills; D3D12, Metal and WebGPU backends |\n| M1 | indie-2d-tools builds | Also version control (joins M2) and AI-assisted authoring (joins M5) |\n| M2 | Standard 3D | ML inference runtime (joins M5) |\n| M3 | massim configuration closed | All networking skills (join M4) |\n\n**The 12 major findings:**\n- **Staffing independence:** co-hosting \"by workstream\" has no separation-of-duties rule. The agent that owns the schedule also calibrates critics, adjudicates findings and parents the milestone gate.\n- **Reference games under-scoped:** 22 reference games, up to an AAA slice, are owned by one process-only expert. No one owns their game code or content.\n- **Live-title operations:**\n  - Nobody owns the server side of a deploy: server build artifacts, draining servers during rolling updates, SLOs, and non-security incident response.\n  - Nobody owns admin, game-master (GM) and player-support tooling on shipping servers.\n- **Legal/IP:** nothing covers clean-room rules for agents studying other engines' code, provenance scanning of agent-written code, patents, or codec royalties.\n- **Milestone ladder:** it stops at an AAA slice. There is no console cert pass, no patch/DLC rehearsal, and no engine 1.0 or LTS milestone. M1 adds 44 skills at once.\n- **Product → architect contract:** game-team requirements are owned by both the architect and product management, with no contract between them. The architect consumes nothing.\n- **Scale-down errors:** file locking and retained build artifacts are tagged `team-large`, but even a 2–3 person team with binary assets needs both.\n- **Licensee forks:** no owner for teams that modify engine source and must merge each new engine release.\n- **Creator docs:** no documentation or learning owner for artists and designers.\n- **Cross-cutting obligations:** the list lacks localizability and \"what can change after launch without a patch\".\n- **Skill-library upkeep:** nothing owns re-bounding skills or updating SKILL.md files while the engine is being built.\n- **Co-development and outsourcing:** partner access control and vendor content delivery have no owner.\n\n**The 4 minor findings:**\n- The build/release architect's purpose text claims pipeline orchestration, which another skill owns.\n- Nothing covers pre-load with keys released at launch, or protection of unreleased content from datamining.\n- There is no program cost ledger (agent compute, CI, device farm, load-test hosting).\n- (Finding 8 in the file also asks product management to take in field telemetry from shipped titles.)\n\nEach finding in the file includes a concrete proposed data change.\n\nCounts: blocker 1, major 12, minor 4. Findings are at `/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-skills/64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82/scratchpad/r2/engine-skill-framework/gauntlet/round-2/K-PROD.md`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10836,"cache_read_input_tokens":157104,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":10836,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":715,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfY3VEZqTNEHS6kkR8Yx4","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"38153953-8563-4113-88e9-6ea8235d8376","timestamp":"2026-09-29T16:26:39.639Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1","slug":"warm-pondering-kernighan"}
